course: dictionary
lesson: 6217
title: Meaning lost in translation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To mistranslate is to change words from one language into another in the wrong way, so the meaning changes. «The tongue map came from a 1901 German study that was mistranslated.» The study was carried into English wrongly, so its message changed.
explain: Word-by-word translation often goes wrong, because a word can look like another word and still mean something different. When you read a translated text, ask: does this make sense in the real world? If a sentence seems strange, the translation may have gone wrong.
explain: Clues in the sentence help you spot the problem. Words like «mistranslated» tell you the original message was carried across badly. Try the swap test: put «translated wrongly» in place of mistranslated and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: To translate means to change words from one language into another.
fact: To mistranslate means to translate wrongly, so the meaning changes.
fact: «Mistranslated» is the past form, as in «a mistranslated German study».
fact: A false friend is a word that looks like a word in another language but means something different: French «librairie» means bookshop, not library.
fact: In news and history, mistranslated messages have caused confusion.
exercise: What does mistranslate mean? | *To translate words wrongly, so the meaning changes | To learn a new language at school | To say the same words twice | To write a book in English
exercise: In French, «librairie» means what? | A library | A French lesson | *A bookshop | A railway station
exercise: Find and copy one word from «The tongue map came from a mistranslated German study.» that means translated wrongly. | from | study | *mistranslated | German
test: Why can a word-by-word translation go wrong? | *Because words that look alike can mean different things in another language | Because each word always means the same in every language | Because some languages have no words | Because translators never use dictionaries
test: In «a mistranslated German study», what has happened to the study? | It was written in German only | It was read aloud in class | It was printed in 1901 by mistake | *It was translated into another language in the wrong way
exam: What is a false friend? | *A word that looks like a word in another language but means something different | A word that is the same in every language | A friend who speaks two languages | A translator who never makes mistakes
